## Customer Churn Prediction using Python & Machine Learning

Developed an end-to-end **Customer Churn Prediction system** to identify customers who are likely to leave a business. The project covers the complete machine-learning workflow, from data preprocessing and exploratory analysis to model training, evaluation, serialization, and deployment through an interactive application.

### Key Features

* Data cleaning and preprocessing
* Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
* Missing-value and duplicate handling
* Feature engineering
* Categorical-data encoding
* Numerical feature preprocessing
* Train/test data splitting
* Machine-learning model development
* Model performance evaluation
* Hyperparameter tuning
* Customer churn prediction
* Prediction pipeline
* Model serialization using Pickle
* Interactive prediction interface
* Data visualization and business insights

### Technologies Used

**Programming:** Python
**Data Analysis:** Pandas, NumPy
**Machine Learning:** Scikit-learn
**Visualization:** Matplotlib, Seaborn
**Web Applications:** Streamlit, Flask
**Model Deployment:** Pickle / joblib

### Machine-Learning Workflow

1. Load and understand the customer dataset
2. Clean and preprocess the data
3. Perform exploratory data analysis
4. Identify important churn-related features
5. Encode categorical variables
6. Prepare training and testing datasets
7. Train machine-learning models
8. Evaluate model performance using appropriate metrics
9. Select and tune the best-performing model
10. Save the trained model
11. Build a prediction pipeline
12. Develop an interactive prediction application
13. Generate visualizations and actionable insights

### Deliverables

* Clean and well-structured Python source code
* Preprocessed dataset
* Exploratory data analysis
* Data visualizations
* Trained machine-learning model
* Serialized `.pkl` / `.joblib` model
* Customer churn prediction pipeline
* Interactive Streamlit application
* Flask-based prediction API/application
* Project documentation
* Setup and execution instructions

### Business Value

The solution helps businesses **identify customers at high risk of churn**, understand important factors influencing customer retention, and support data-driven customer-retention strategies.

The project demonstrates practical experience in **Data Science, Machine Learning, Data Analysis, Feature Engineering, Model Deployment, and Python application development**.

Evaluation Metrics

The model is evaluated using:

Accuracy
Precision
Recall
F1 Score
ROC-AUC
Confusion Matrix





